        "falseColor": false,
        "notes": "Convex light-curve reconstruction, 147 ± 32 km volume-equivalent diameter in the selected archive record. No surface imagery exists; rotational phase is illustrative. The original mesh is uniformly scaled to the selected archive record’s declared volume-equivalent diameter. Published ensemble estimates can differ from this archived solution. Original coordinates and connectivity are retained; no albedo, craters or regolith are inferred. One mean color for the whole disc (Gaia DR3 reflectance spectrum), scaled to the 5.8% geometric albedo JPL lists; no terrain, albedo pattern or color variation is drawn."
